 has a feasible point whose value is below the optimum of (P).","When (P) has an optimal solution, the smallest value of (D) is attained and equals the largest value of (P)."],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a268ae25937543b6005a65d9","time_limit":40,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-11-12T08:25:14.320156+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"},{"id":"year_2_1b_math_vi_convexity_and_optimization_strong_duality_24efbdb6_010","difficulty":"basic","question_type":"application","question":"The linear program (P) $\\max 2x_1+5x_2$ subject to $x_1+x_2\\leq6$, $x_1+3x_2\\leq12$, $\\boldsymbol{x}\\geq\\boldsymbol{0}$ has dual (D) $\\min 6y_1+12y_2$ subject to $y_1+y_2\\geq2$, $y_1+3y_2\\geq5$, $\\boldsymbol{y}\\geq\\boldsymbol{0}$, and (D) has the optimal solution $\\boldsymbol{y}^{\\ast}=(\\tfrac{1}{2},\\tfrac{3}{2})$. What is the optimal value of (P)?","options":["$-21$","$21$","$15$","$\\tfrac{17}{2}$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"a2190c95a3244f67c3ae3f58","time_limit":35,"curation_status":"retired","retired_at":"2026-11-12T09:28:08.193334+00:00","reason_code":"duplicate_diagnostic_target"}]}}